    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d626">

                <pb facs="0769" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.9131/93</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 359</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-14">February 14, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reference is made to the first paragraph of
                    the Department’s telegram No. 8, of February 10, 1938, in which it was stated
                    that copies of the standard draft of general provisions for inclusion in trade
                    agreements would be sent you. There are enclosed herewith copies of these
                    provisions for transmittal to the Iranian Government. For your information and
                    guidance, there are also enclosed copies of a memorandum<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d626-f1"/> explaining the general objective of the draft article
                    relating to foreign exchange control and the purpose of the specific assurances
                    it provides. It is believed that certain parts of this memorandum will be of
                    assistance to you in explaining the purpose of this provision to the Iranian
                    Government. There are also enclosed, for such use as you deem advisable in your
                    conversations with the Iranian authorities, copies of a memorandum<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d626-f2"/> explaining the procedure followed by this Government in
                    connection with trade-agreement negotiations and the Department’s preliminary
                    and formal announcements with regard to negotiations with Turkey.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis
                            B. Sayre</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
